{
 "_comment": "Genesis seed pack (English) for the action map (V2-539). Same rules as es.json: unambiguous whole-utterance commands only; variants are separate entries; anything that could mean more than the mapped action stays out and goes to the model. · V2-682 — the possessive and the courtesy form were the whole hole. Measured on the operator's own English session (2026-09-12): «open the agenda» matched and «can you open MY agenda, please» did not, so a widget SHOW fell through to the model and from there to a Brain Worker that died on a provider 400. Spanish had the identical hole («abre mi agenda», «abreme la agenda»), which is why the fix lands in BOTH packs: this was never an English defect. Courtesy and modal forms are ENTRIES here, never something the matcher is allowed to understand (normalize.py doctrine). · V2-761 — the widget catalogue («Apps») joins as a panel tab; the operator calls it apps or widgets indifferently, so both words are entries.",
 "version": 10,
 "grids": [
  {
   "_comment": "VERB x OBJECT grid for mensajeria's LENSES (V2-545). «Abreme el Telegram» is not «show the card»: WhatsApp/Telegram/correo are VIEWS OF a card, and the model reads them as card names because they are also the widget's aliases - measured live, three turns of «Aqui lo tienes» over an unmoved card. Expanded into ordinary exact-match entries at import; a view op also brings the card up (executor), so one order gets both halves. `$` is filled with the value.",
